      "content": "The scientific consensus acknowledges that there is ongoing debate and some inconsistencies in research. However, the majority of the scientific community recognizes that gender identity is a complex phenomenon that cannot be reduced solely to biological sex or purely as a social construct. Many experts agree that the ideology that gender is an all-or-nothing, biologically determined binary is not supported by empirical evidence. Instead, most researchers view gender as a spectrum, influenced by a variety of biological, psychological, and social factors.",
